        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "873ccfd1-d925-5a57-8687-65da6db5d51b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Courtney Love, Steven Baigelman, Keanu Reeves, Vincent D'Onofrio, Cameron Diaz, Tuesday Weld, Dan Aykroyd, Delroy Lindo, Dave Callahan, Paul Clark, Andy Golding, Andy Bolton, Frank Stebbing\n- Organizations: Hole, The Wolfhounds\n- Places: Romford, UK\n- Products: Feeling Minnesota\n- Topics: alternative rock, indie pop, noise pop\n\nFacts:\n- Courtney Love was born Courtney Michelle Harrison on July 9, 1964, and she is an American singer, songwriter, actress, and visual artist.\n- The Wolfhounds are an indie pop and noise pop band that formed in Romford, UK, in 1985, founded by Dave Callahan, Paul Clark, Andy Golding, Andy Bolton, and Frank Stebbing, and the band was originally active until 1990.\n- Courtney Love formed the alternative rock band Hole in 1989 and rose to prominence as its frontwoman.\n- Feeling Minnesota is a 1996 American crime drama comedy film written and directed by Steven Baigelman.\n- Feeling Minnesota stars Keanu Reeves, Vincent D'Onofrio, Cameron Diaz, Tuesday Weld, Dan Aykroyd, Delroy Lindo, and Courtney Love.",
